  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find $2det(A)+4det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\ndet(A)=1\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot 1=4\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has two identical rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2det(A)+4det(B)=2\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 0=8.$",
